From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exynos6694 <azsx6694@naver.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:04:07 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Animal Crossing: a picture wider than 16:9 for an iPhone in
 landscape (screen_aspect wide)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An iPhone in landscape is about 2.17:1, and the 16:9 picture left a band at each side. A profile with
screen_aspect wide now follows DM_SCREEN_ASPECT above 1.79 (to 2.5; iOS's Match screen passes the
window's shape): the output keeps 16:9's height and grows sideways (2.167 → 2352x1080, a 1568x720
layout space; loader.c state +0x64..+0x70, the HUD's side shift at +0x9c..+0xa4). +0x48 stays 0, so a
taller screen's path is untouched.

Animal Crossing: New Horizons 3.0.3 (patches.py): each screen-shape stub takes the taller path when
+0x48 is set, the wider one when +0x64 is, else the original instructions (assembled; the source is
quoted). Wider: the display size's width from its height, the layout sizes' 1280 the layout width,
the resolution entry and the layouts' DrawInfo the framebuffer's width, a 16:9 layout projection's x
row divided by the stretch; the cameras keep their vertical angle, so the scene shows more at the
sides. duo_anchor.c stretches full-screen backgrounds sideways and moves a widget at |x| 300 or more
(DM_SCREEN_HUD_SIDE) out by the extra half-width. game.py / hle_profile take screen_aspect wide (2).

Checked on a Mac (M3 Pro, macOS 27.2) at 2.167: the title, the island, the phone and the pockets in
their own shape, the HUD and button guides at the sides; 1.43 renders as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Animal Crossing on an iPhone in landscape: a picture wider than 16:9 instead of side bands
Issue: none yet (exynos6694/NX2Apple-muti feature/local-wireless)

